# Docker build context excludes (repo root). Keep this generous but careful:
# apps/api/Dockerfile explicitly COPYs only the package.json files + source
# directories it needs, so excluding apps/mobile's heavy native/build output
# here is safe as long as apps/mobile/package.json itself stays reachable
# (it is — only its subdirectories are excluded below, not the whole folder).

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

.git
.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.expo

# Prisma client is generated inside the Docker build itself.
apps/api/src/generated

# Mobile native/build artifacts — never needed to build @sp/api.
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/builds
apps/mobile/expo-env.d.ts
*.apk
*.aab

# Local dev data / infra (D:\dev, embedded Postgres, SeaweedFS) never lives
# in the repo tree, but exclude the usual local-data markers defensively.
.data
*.log

# Secrets — never bake real env values into an image layer.
# Bare patterns only match at the context root in Docker's ignore matching
# (unlike gitignore), so nested .env files (e.g. apps/api/.env) need an
# explicit **/ prefix or they slip through into the build context.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Docs/design assets irrelevant to the API build.
docs
design-system
social_publishing_app_blueprint_v2.md
README.md
